From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:06:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] waylandhost: add a compositor for client surfaces and
 kodi_web_v1

CWaylandHost is a Wayland compositor without a screen of its own. It
spawns its clients with an inherited socket and serves wl_compositor,
xdg_wm_base, linux-dmabuf, wp_presentation, a seat that forwards
Kodi's input, and text-input-v3 so that Kodi's keyboard can type into
a client. Committed client buffers are handed to an observer, which
shows them through Kodi's renderers, and the observer learns when a
surface goes away. When the host stops, its clients get SIGTERM and
their exit is awaited; a client still running 90 s later, for instance
one blocked on a stale network mount, is killed. Clients learn the
screen's mode, and when the display is reset for a new mode every
output gets the new mode and every surface a configure for the new
size.

The host also serves kodi_web_v1, a protocol through which Kodi drives a
web browser it hosts: the browser creates one view per profile, a
hermetic set of cookies and storage, only when Kodi asks for it. Kodi
configures each view with a user agent, the viewport its pages are
written for, user scripts and content filters before it loads a URL,
navigates it, learns its URL, title, load progress, errors, media state
and requests to leave, and closes it when done. Content filters use the
Adblock Plus filter syntax, so that one maintained list serves any
engine.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
